# aida-negation-spelling-in-unfolding inside ONE argument (found 2026-10-21
# on Tweety's PlExample): the declared rule spells the negation A -> false,
# the inline proof of it spells ~A (cut (~A) x, c3 : B -> ~A). `check`
# accepts it, `graph c` (and label/evaluate) is refused: "Fellowship
# rejected the unfolded term for 'c': a is neither in your hypothesis nor
# in your conclusion". Spelled ~A throughout (as in tweety/logic, not_a)
# the same proof labels IN and evaluates to a value.
lk.
declare A, B, C : bool.
declare c1 : ((A -> false) -> C).
declare c2 : (A -> B).
declare c3 : (B -> ~A).
argument c : (C).
cut ((A -> false) -> C) th.
axiom c1.
elim.
elim a.
cut (~A) x.
cut (B -> ~A) t1.
axiom c3.
elim.
cut (A -> B) t2.
axiom c2.
elim.
axiom a.
axiom t2.
axiom t1.
elim.
axiom.
axiom th.
dixi.
